*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Identify the point of tangency between the two circles ($z = 2$).
2. Apply a Möbius map with pole at $z = 2$ to map the region between tangent circles to a parallel strip.
3. Scale and rotate the strip to the standard horizontal strip $0 < "Im" < pi$.
4. Apply the complex exponential function to map the strip onto the upper half plane.
